/// Datasheet for the `textedit` element device — a multi-line code editor. The device owns NO storage; the
/// DRIVER owns the columns and the selected backend edits + renders them. Decoupled from `gfx`: the window
/// backend does the editing ITSELF from a driver-provided key (`{ukey}`, filled from gfx.key) and blits into the
/// shared `{framebuffer}`; the dom backend is a real `<textarea>`. Columns the driver provides:
///   {ebuf, elen, ecur}     the edit buffer, its live length, and the cursor index
///   {submit}               raised to 1 on Ctrl-R / ⌘-Enter — the driver reads it to run/act
///   {evx, evy, evw, evh}   the editor's screen rect (render px)
///   {ukey}                 one key per frame (ASCII or a gfx sentinel; the driver fills from gfx.key)
///   {vpw, vph}             viewport size for framebuffer stride/clip (window only)
///
/// Backends: `window` (framebuffer editor: `step` edits, `render` blits text + cursor) and `dom` (a `<textarea>`:
/// `text` pulls its value into `{ebuf}`, `poll_run` reports ⌘-Enter). Pick with `[select] textedit =
/// "window" | "dom"`. Part of the `ui` element family; builds on the shared `ui` core (extras/ui/ui/).
// RUN: true
